    "result_text": "Tests pass. Both findings addressed:\n\n**Finding 1 (duplicated canonical path)** \u2014 Agreed and fixed by making `selfLink` the single source of truth. The mapper is now the sole place that composes `\"/api/owners/\" + id`; `RespondWithOwnerCreated` maps the DTO first and sources its `201` Location from `dto.getSelfLink()` (`URI.create(dto.getSelfLink())`) instead of re-deriving the string. I chose this over a separate `OwnerPath.of(...)` helper because the responder already has the mapped DTO in hand, so no new type is needed and the two literals genuinely collapse to one. At that point the owner is persisted and has an id, so `getSelfLink()` is always non-null.\n\n**Finding 2 (comment detached from annotation)** \u2014 Agreed and fixed; each rationale now sits directly above the `@Mapping` it describes, with the `selfLink` comment between the two stacked annotations.\n\nI kept the inline ternary as the review noted that asymmetry is acceptable. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
