    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe mapper is the right boundary for a derived presentation field, and placing `selfLink` next to `identityKey` fits the documented \"single Owner-to-DTO boundary\" pattern. But the change introduces a duplicated source of truth.\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 Duplicated canonical owner path (the main issue).**\n`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java:17` already builds the identical string for the `201` Location header:\n```java\nresponse.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create(\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId())).body(dto));\n```\nAfter this change, the exact same `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` is also computed in `OwnerMapper.java:27`. The new field even documents itself as \"The canonical path to this owner\" \u2014 which is semantically the *same* value as the created Location. So the canonical owner path now has two independent definitions (same literal prefix, same concatenation) that must be kept in sync by hand; change the base path and you have to remember both.\n\nThis codebase already establishes the idiom for exactly this situation: the sibling derivation is extracted into `OwnerIdentity.of(owner)` rather than inlined. Follow that pattern here \u2014 put the path derivation in one place (e.g. an `OwnerPath.of(owner)` helper in `rest.function.owner`, mirroring `OwnerIdentity`) and have both the mapper expression and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` use it. Simpler still: since `RespondWithOwnerCreated` already maps the DTO before setting the header, it can source the Location from `dto.getSelfLink()`, making `selfLink` the single source of truth. Either way, the two literals should collapse to one.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 Minor: comment block no longer pairs with its annotation.**\nAt `OwnerMapper.java:22-27` the two comment paragraphs are now stacked above *both* `@Mapping` lines, so the identityKey comment and the selfLink comment read as one block detached from the annotations they each describe. A comment can sit directly between the stacked annotations:\n```java\n// identityKey comment \u2026\n@Mapping(target = \"identityKey\", \u2026)\n// selfLink comment \u2026\n@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", \u2026)\n```\nKeeps each rationale next to the mapping it explains.\n\nNote the inline ternary (vs. a helper like `identityKey` uses) is acceptable on its own \u2014 the expression is trivial \u2014 so that asymmetry isn't the problem; the duplication across `RespondWithOwnerCreated` is.",
